{"user": "wait, can you walk me through why g2 ended up flipping that whole column - was that the key swing move?", "user_ts": "2026-08-13T06:23:38.837426+00:00", "assistant": "Yes \u2014 **g2 was a big swing because it \u201cbracketed\u201d the g-column**.\n\nIn Othello, a move flips a line if your new disc and another one of your discs trap opponent discs between them.\n\nSo when **Black plays g2**, if the column looked like:\n\n**g2 = Black move**, then **g3\u2013g7 = White**, and **g8 = Black**\n\nthen Black brackets the whole vertical line:\n\n**g2 Black \u2026 g3-g7 White \u2026 g8 Black**\n\nSo **g3, g4, g5, g6, g7 all flip to Black** at once.\n\nThat was likely the key swing: not because g2 is a corner or stable, but because it created a long vertical flip and changed a lot of discs near the end, when there\u2019s little time for White to flip them back.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-13T06:23:38.837426+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-13T06:23:43.837426+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3, "Common Ground Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0, "Common Ground Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"], "gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle", "Positive Feedback"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle", "Positive Feedback"], "votes": {"Worked Line": 1, "General Principle": 2, "Paraphrase": 1, "Positive Feedback": 2, "Board Report": 2, "Local Justification": 2}, "confidence": {"Worked Line